  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="35">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 35</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="35">[Not in D]</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="35" corresp="#wit-k">⁊ gif hwa of fyrde butan leafe gewende þe cyning sylf on sy, plihte his are.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">And if anyone deserts an army which is under the personal command of the king, it shall be at the risk of losing his property.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wenn einer ohne Erlaubniss von der Landwehr, bei der der König selbst ist, fortgeht, bringe er seiner Besitzstellung Gefahr der Verwirkung.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if anyone leaves the army without permission when the king himself is with it, let him put his whole property at risk of forfeiture.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Only in K. Liebermann compares V Atr 28.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
